---
const title = 'About USIVA | A US Council Planning Companion';
const description = 'Learn how USIVA fits beside US Council and US Fellows as an informational visa-readiness and compliance-planning companion for international study and research pathways.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/about.html';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://usiva.org/assets/usiva-social.svg" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="USIVA — visa-readiness and compliance planning" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4efe5" />
  </head>
  <body class="about-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="topline"><div class="about-wrap"><span>U.S. Immigration &amp; Visa Association</span><a href="https://usfellows.org/international-rd-scholars.html">US Fellows / International R&amp;D Scholars ↗</a></div></div>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="about-wrap header-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="USIVA home"><span class="brand-seal" aria-hidden="true">US</span><span><strong>USIVA</strong><small>A US Council companion</small></span></a>
        <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
          <a href="/services.html">Services</a>
          <a href="/about.html" aria-current="page">About</a>
          <a href="/pricing.html">Scope &amp; fees</a>
          <a href="/blog.html">Field notes</a>
          <a class="nav-cta" href="/contacts.html">Start a question</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="about-opening">
        <div class="about-wrap opening-grid">
          <div class="opening-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">About / the short version</p>
            <h1>The companion that keeps visa questions in the room.</h1>
            <p class="opening-lede">USIVA is the U.S. Immigration and Visa Association: a US Council companion for visa-readiness and compliance planning around international study, research, and related pathways.</p>
            <div class="opening-actions"><a class="button button--ink" href="/services.html">See the planning lanes</a><a class="under-link" href="/other-pages.html">Open the route atlas <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="origin-slip" aria-label="USIVA relationship map">
            <p class="slip-label">Relationship map</p>
            <p class="slip-line"><span>US Council</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>USIVA</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>US Fellows</span></p>
            <p>One public information layer can connect the research pathway to the questions that surround status, documentation, timing, and authorization.</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--quiet" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
        <div class="about-wrap essay-grid">
          <p class="margin-note">01<br />WHY THIS SITE EXISTS</p>
          <div class="essay-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">A practical role</p>
            <h2 id="why-heading">Ambition is easier to protect when the compliance question arrives early.</h2>
            <p>International candidates often have to hold several timelines at once: academic preparation, funding, travel, school instructions, research opportunities, and the authorization boundaries that apply to each stage. USIVA gives those questions a visible place in the conversation before deadline pressure makes them harder to separate.</p>
            <p>The site is intentionally planning-oriented. It can help a reader name a missing document, prepare a question for a designated school official or sponsor, and identify when a personal situation should be taken to licensed immigration counsel. It does not decide eligibility or replace the authority responsible for a case.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="role-section" aria-labelledby="role-heading">
        <div class="about-wrap">
          <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Two connected roles</p>
            <h2 id="role-heading">The research pathway and the visa-readiness file should inform each other.</h2>
            <p>USIVA and US Fellows are linked here because a candidate may need both kinds of preparation. The responsibilities are different, and neither page can promise the result controlled by a school, sponsor, government agency, or attorney.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="role-map">
            <article class="role-card role-card--research">
              <span class="role-tag">US Fellows</span>
              <h3>Research pathway</h3>
              <p>The US Fellows public pathway describes research direction, university preparation, professor and partner conversations, and a route toward the International R&amp;D Scholars Program.</p>
              <a href="https://usfellows.org/international-rd-scholars.html">View the US Fellows pathway ↗</a>
            </article>
            <article class="role-card role-card--visa">
              <span class="role-tag">USIVA</span>
              <h3>Visa-readiness planning</h3>
              <p>USIVA keeps documentation, timing, work-authorization boundaries, status questions, and escalation points visible alongside that research conversation.</p>
              <a href="/services.html">Explore USIVA planning ↗</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
        <div class="about-wrap principles-grid">
          <div class="principles-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">The editorial standard</p>
            <h2 id="principles-heading">Four habits keep a planning page honest.</h2>
            <p>These are working principles for public information, not claims about a particular person’s case.</p>
          </div>
          <ol class="principles-list">
            <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Start with the decision</h3><p>Ask what must be decided, by whom, and by when before collecting an indiscriminate stack of documents.</p></div></li>
            <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Make the boundary explicit</h3><p>Study, training, research exposure, assistantship, travel, and employment can have different rules. Name the activity before assuming it is allowed.</p></div></li>
            <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Leave a source trail</h3><p>Public rules, school instructions, sponsor guidance, and professional advice should be checked at the point of use and dated.</p></div></li>
            <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Know when to hand off</h3><p>Personal history, a prior refusal, a status concern, or a complicated work question deserves individualized advice from the right authority.</p></div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="plain-language" aria-labelledby="plain-heading">
        <div class="about-wrap plain-language__grid">
          <div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Plain language</p><h2 id="plain-heading">What USIVA is — and what this site is not.</h2></div>
          <div class="plain-columns">
            <div><h3>USIVA is</h3><ul><li>A public planning companion for international study and research questions.</li><li>A place to organize records, timing, source checks, and handoffs.</li><li>A bridge to the US Fellows research-pathway conversation.</li></ul></div>
            <div><h3>USIVA is not</h3><ul><li>A guarantee of admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, or government approval.</li><li>A substitute for university, sponsor, consular, government, or legal instructions.</li><li>A public case file, legal opinion, or promise that a pathway is available.</li></ul></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section--quiet" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
        <div class="about-wrap next-panel">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Continue with a purpose</p><h2 id="next-heading">Choose the page that answers your next question.</h2></div>
          <div class="next-links"><a href="/services.html"><span>01</span><strong>Organize a planning question</strong><em>Services →</em></a><a href="/tips-faq.html"><span>02</span><strong>Check a common boundary</strong><em>Tips &amp; FAQ →</em></a><a href="/contacts.html"><span>03</span><strong>Prepare a careful handoff</strong><em>Contacts →</em></a></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="notice"><div class="about-wrap"><strong>Important notice:</strong> USIVA content is informational planning content. It does not provide individualized legal advice or guarantee admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, or government approval.</div></section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="about-wrap footer-grid">
        <div><a class="footer-brand" href="/">USIVA</a><p>Visa-readiness and compliance planning for international study and research pathways.</p></div>
        <div><p class="footer-label">Explore</p><a href="/services.html">Services</a><a href="/pricing.html">Scope &amp; fees</a><a href="/blog.html">Field notes</a></div>
        <div><p class="footer-label">Questions</p><a href="/tips-faq.html">Tips &amp; FAQ</a><a href="/contacts.html">Start a question</a><a href="/media-gallery.html">Media &amp; field notes</a></div>
        <div><p class="footer-label">Notice</p><p>USIVA is a US Council companion site. Verify current instructions with the authority responsible for your situation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="about-wrap footer-bottom">© 2026 USIVA · A US Council companion site.</div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; background: #fbfaf7; color: #172231; font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; line-height: 1.65; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
  :global(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  :global(a:focus-visible), :global(summary:focus-visible) { outline: 3px solid #c59d54; outline-offset: 4px; }
  :global(p) { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: #5c6974; }
  :global(h1), :global(h2), :global(h3) { margin: 0 0 .7rem; color: #0a253f; font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.08; }
  :global(h1) { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7.3vw, 7rem); letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  :global(h2) { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.2vw, 4.25rem); letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  :global(h3) { font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.7rem); }
  .about-wrap { width: min(1160px, calc(100% - 48px)); margin-inline: auto; }
  .skip-link { position: fixed; top: -4rem; left: 1rem; z-index: 20; padding: .7rem 1rem; background: #fff; color: #0a253f; font-weight: 800; }
  .skip-link:focus { top: 1rem; }
  .topline { background: #0a253f; color: #e6eef1; font-size: .77rem; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .topline .about-wrap { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding-block: .55rem; }
  .topline a { color: #efd69b; font-weight: 800; }
  .site-header { background: #fbfaf7; border-bottom: 1px solid #d8dfe1; }
  .header-inner { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 2rem; min-height: 5.6rem; }
  .brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; }
  .brand-seal { display: grid; width: 2.8rem; height: 2.8rem; place-items: center; border: 1px solid #b9893e; border-radius: 50%; color: #0a253f; font: 700 .8rem Georgia, serif; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px #fbfaf7, inset 0 0 0 5px #b9893e; }
  .brand strong { display: block; color: #0a253f; font: 700 1.5rem/1 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .brand small { display: block; color: #52616a; font-size: .58rem; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-end; gap: .3rem 1.25rem; color: #334350; font-size: .84rem; font-weight: 750; }
  nav a:hover, nav a[aria-current="page"] { color: #ae403a; }
  .nav-cta { padding: .55rem .8rem; border: 1px solid #ae403a; color: #ae403a; }
  .about-opening { background: #f4efe5; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd4c7; }
  .opening-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(18rem, .8fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 9rem); align-items: end; min-height: 39rem; padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  .opening-copy { max-width: 56rem; }
  .eyebrow, .slip-label, .footer-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: #ae403a; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .opening-lede { max-width: 45rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: #40515b; font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.5; }
  .opening-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 3rem; padding: .75rem 1.05rem; border: 1px solid #0a253f; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .button--ink { background: #0a253f; color: #fff; }
  .under-link { color: #ae403a; font-size: .87rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .origin-slip { align-self: center; padding: 1.75rem; border: 1px solid #cdbf9c; border-top: 5px solid #c59d54; background: #fffdf9; transform: rotate(1.2deg); box-shadow: .9rem .9rem 0 rgba(10,37,63,.08); }
  .origin-slip p:last-child { margin: 0; font-size: .9rem; }
  .slip-label { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: #ae403a; }
  .slip-line { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; color: #0a253f; font: 700 1.05rem Georgia, serif; }
  .slip-line b { color: #ae403a; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; }
  .section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem); }
  .section--quiet { background: #f8f9f8; border-block: 1px solid #e0e6e5; }
  .essay-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, .3fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 9rem); }
  .margin-note { margin: .4rem 0 0; color: #ae403a; font: 700 .72rem/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .essay-copy { max-width: 49rem; }
  .essay-copy p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 1.08rem; }
  .role-section { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7rem); background: #0a253f; color: #fff; }
  .section-intro { max-width: 55rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .section-intro h2 { color: #fff; }
  .section-intro p:last-child { color: #d4e0e5; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .eyebrow--light { color: #efd69b; }
  .role-map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.25); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25); }
  .role-card { min-height: 20rem; padding: 2rem; background: #123957; }
  .role-card--visa { background: #1b605c; }
  .role-tag { display: block; margin-bottom: 4rem; color: #efd69b; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .role-card h3 { color: #fff; font-size: 2.3rem; }
  .role-card p { color: #d9e4e8; }
  .role-card a { display: inline-block; margin-top: .7rem; color: #fff; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .principles-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 8rem); }
  .principles-intro { max-width: 28rem; }
  .principles-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid #cbd5d6; }
  .principles-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5d6; }
  .principles-list li > span { color: #ae403a; font: 700 .78rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .principles-list h3 { margin-bottom: .35rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .principles-list p { margin: 0; }
  .plain-language { padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); background: #071827; color: #fff; }
  .plain-language__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: 4rem; }
  .plain-language h2 { color: #fff; }
  .plain-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  .plain-columns > div { padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 2px solid #c59d54; }
  .plain-columns h3 { color: #fff; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .plain-columns ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.15rem; color: #d1dee4; }
  .plain-columns li { margin: .75rem 0; }
  .next-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr); gap: 3rem; align-items: end; }
  .next-links { border-top: 1px solid #cbd5d6; }
  .next-links a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr auto; gap: .8rem; align-items: center; padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5d6; }
  .next-links span { color: #ae403a; font: 700 .75rem ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .next-links strong { color: #0a253f; }
  .next-links em { color: #ae403a; font-size: .78rem; font-style: normal; font-weight: 850; }
  .notice { padding-block: 1.2rem; background: #f8e7be; color: #36280e; font-size: .88rem; }
  .site-footer { padding-block: 4rem 1.5rem; background: #0b2238; color: #cad7df; }
  .footer-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .7fr .8fr 1.1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  .footer-brand { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: .8rem; color: #fff; font: 700 1.55rem Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .site-footer p { color: #b5c5cf; font-size: .86rem; }
  .site-footer a { display: block; margin: .35rem 0; color: #d9e4e9; font-size: .86rem; }
  .site-footer a:hover { color: #f0d798; }
  .footer-label { margin-bottom: .7rem; color: #efd69b; }
  .footer-bottom { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16); color: #8ea3b0; font-size: .78rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .header-inner { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; padding-block: 1rem; }
    nav { justify-content: flex-start; }
    .opening-grid, .principles-grid, .plain-language__grid, .next-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .origin-slip { max-width: 32rem; }
    .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about-wrap { width: min(100% - 2rem, 1160px); }
    .topline .about-wrap { display: block; }
    .topline a { display: inline-block; margin-top: .3rem; }
    .essay-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .role-map, .plain-columns, .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .role-card { min-height: auto; }
    .role-tag { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .next-links a { grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; }
    .next-links em { grid-column: 2; }
    .opening-actions .button { width: 100%; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { :global(html) { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
</style>
